 "phase": "L18 + L19 (loading time and memory), one gate: allocation overlaps by binary search; unwritten Frame slots shared",
 "change": "L18: the catalog attempt checked each allocation against every earlier range with a scan; OriginalAllocationRanges keeps the memory's live allocations at entry (possibly empty or overlapping) sorted with the running maximum end, and the ranges added since (each checked, non-empty, disjoint) sorted, answering the same predicate (lo < r.hi && r.lo < hi) by binary search; the unused checkingOverlap parameter is gone. L19: after parsing an object the loader built a record and a projection for all 400 Frame slots; a slot no frame wrote depends only on its backing slice (box counts 0, no sound pointer), so slots with the same slice share one record and one projection, renumbered (OriginalFrameRecord.number is internally settable).",
 "why one gate": "L19's memory effect is deterministic (Mac heap: Frame records 26.7 -> 7.6 MB, projection arrays 23.4 -> 6.6 MB; 15,478 of 54,800 slots written); the A12 L16 profile attributes the time: the overlap scan ~9% and the unwritten slots' records and projections ~6% of the catalog window",
 "review": "independent read-only reviewer: no bug (L18 exact for empty and overlapping base ranges, the added ranges stay sorted and disjoint, nothing else read the old array; L19 values equal for any backing including nil, projections of unwritten slots read only their record, error order unchanged, sharing safe for every consumer); follow-ups applied before the gate: sharesStorage(with:) instead of forced identities, a nil-backing test case, test registrations",
 "notes": "One L19 phone run re-extracted the assets after its install (22.3 s startup, S2).",
